v 3
d ivmediate: causal mediation analysis for linear IV models with a single instrument
d
d Decomposes the effect of a treatment T on an outcome Y into a direct
d effect and an indirect effect through a mediator M, using one or more
d instruments for T and no separate instrument for M (Ferrara, Gold,
d Heblich, and Pinto 2026). Reports the Olea-Pflueger effective F,
d Anderson-Rubin confidence sets, and kappa- and R-squared-based
d sensitivity analyses; supports one- and two-way absorbed fixed
d effects, weights, robust, cluster and Conley standard errors,
d post-double-selection LASSO, and the bootstrap.
d
d Version 2.0.0; replaces ivmediate 1.0.4 (SSC, 2020).
d Requires Stata 16 or later.
d
d Authors: Andreas Ferrara (maintainer, a.ferrara@pitt.edu),
d Robert Gold, Stephan Heblich, Rodrigo Pinto
d License: MIT. Copyright (c) 2026 Andreas Ferrara, Robert Gold,
d Stephan Heblich, Rodrigo Pinto
d Source and issues: https://github.com/aferrara87/ivmediate
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261017
f ivmediate.ado
f ivmediate.sthlp
